# Architecture & UI Defect List

**Audit Date:** 2026-06-13
**Re-validated:** 2026-06-13 (second pass correcting MED-01, HIGH-03, MED-05)
**Inspector:** ARCHITECTURE AUDITOR 9000
**Scope:** TypeScript/TSX code quality, UI component architecture, spec compliance, wiring defects, regression risks
**Packages Examined:** `packages/{tui,ui,app,opencode,cli,enterprise}`
**Typecheck Status:** ✅ All packages typecheck clean (`bun typecheck` exits 0 on all 5 packages)

---

## How to Read This

Each defect has:
- **ID** — unique reference
- **Severity** — Critical / High / Medium / Low / Cosmetic
- **Confidence** — Confirmed / Likely / Suspected
- **Category** — see classification below
- **Evidence** — file paths, line numbers, code excerpts
- **Spec Reference** — if a written spec is violated
- **Impact** — what breaks or is at risk
- **Recommendation** — minimal surgical fix

### Category Legend

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| ARC | Architecture Gap — wrong layer, wrong boundary, wrong ownership |
| WIR | Wiring Defect — broken chain, mismatched import, stale reference |
| ERR | Error Handling Defect — swallowed exceptions, missing `.catch()`, silent failure |
| STD | Standards Drift — inconsistent coding conventions, style conflicts |
| FRG | Runtime Fragility — fragile assumptions, temporal coupling |
| OBS | Observability Gap — can't diagnose what's happening |
| DUP | Dead Code or Duplicate System — two implementations of the same thing |
| SPEC | Spec Violation — code breaks a documented invariant |

