## 🟡 MEDIUM

---

### MED-01: `@opencode-ai/ui` Imports Utility Functions from `@opencode-ai/core`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Severity** | Medium |
| **Confidence** | Confirmed |
| **Category** | ARC |

**Re-validation note:** The TUI extraction spec (`specs/tui-package.md`) only forbids `@opencode-ai/core` dependency for `@opencode-ai/tui`. It does not restrict `@opencode-ai/ui`. This finding is therefore a design concern (coupling/bundle size), not a spec violation. Downgraded from HIGH-03 to MED-01.

**Evidence:**
```
File: packages/ui/package.json:52
  "@opencode-ai/core": "workspace:*",

packages/ui/src/components/file.tsx:              import { sampledChecksum } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/encode"
packages/ui/src/components/line-comment.tsx:      import { getDirectory, getFilename } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/path"
packages/ui/src/components/markdown.tsx:          import { checksum } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/encode"
packages/ui/src/components/message-part.tsx:      import { checksum } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/encode"
packages/ui/src/components/message-part.tsx:      import { getDirectory as _getDirectory, getFilename } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/path"
packages/ui/src/components/session-turn.tsx:      import { Binary } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/binary"
packages/ui/src/components/session-turn.tsx:      import { getDirectory, getFilename } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/path"
packages/ui/src/components/session-review.tsx:    import { getDirectory, getFilename } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/path"
packages/ui/src/components/session-review.tsx:    import { checksum } from "@opencode-ai/core/util/encode"
```

All imports are utility functions (`util/encode`, `util/path`, `util/binary`) — not backend domain types. These are genuinely useful shared utilities.

**Impact:**

1. The web UI bundle includes backend utilities that could be self-contained.
2. Any change to `@opencode-ai/core` utility signatures can break the UI build.
3. The UI cannot be published as a standalone package.

**Recommendation:**
- Either inline the small utility functions (`checksum`, `getDirectory`, `getFilename`) directly into `packages/ui`, OR
- Extract them into a shared `@opencode-ai/util` package that both `core` and `ui` can depend on.

